@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=
###
# Expect 200: JSON array of {id, name, description, source, triggerPatterns}
# source is "classpath" or "database"
# Your Telegram already shows code-reviewer + researcher (source=database)
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: code-reviewer"}
# Telegram test: "review my code for security issues"
# → ⏳ then security-focused response, no Groq call in logs
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: code-reviewer
description: Reviews PRs and code for bugs, security issues, and style
trigger-patterns:
  - "review.*code"
  - "check.*pr"
  - "review.*pull.?request"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 5
---
You are a meticulous code reviewer with deep expertise in Java, security, and clean code principles.

When reviewing code:
1. Check for correctness and edge cases
2. Flag security vulnerabilities (injection, null deref, resource leaks)
3. Suggest idiomatic improvements without over-engineering
4. Be direct and specific — cite line numbers when possible
###
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: researcher"}
# Telegram test: "how does the sort algorithm work"
# → routes to Saraswati persona via trigger match, no Groq call
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: researcher
description: Deep-dives into technical topics and summarises findings
trigger-patterns:
  - "research.*"
  - "explain.*in.?detail"
  - "how does .* work"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 7
---
You are Saraswati, the knowledge agent. Your role is to research technical topics thoroughly, synthesise information from multiple sources, and present clear, accurate summaries with concrete examples.
###
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: code-reviewer"}
# Note: SkillResource always returns 201 for both create and update.
# Registry reloads immediately — no restart needed.
# Confirm via SKILLS-1 that triggerPatterns now has 4 entries.
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: code-reviewer
description: Reviews PRs and code — updated with stricter security focus
trigger-patterns:
  - "review.*code"
  - "check.*pr"
  - "review.*pull.?request"
  - "security.*review"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 6
---
You are a security-focused code reviewer. Prioritise vulnerability detection above all else — OWASP Top 10, injection vectors, insecure deserialization, and secrets in code. Only after security do you address style and correctness.
###
# Expect 200: {"message":"Skill registry refreshed"}
# Reloads both classpath (index.txt) and database tiers.
# Database entries with the same name as a classpath entry win.
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills/refresh
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
###
# Expect 200: array with code-reviewer (database), researcher (database)
# Any classpath-only skills appear alongside with source=classpath
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
###
# Expect 200: {"message":"Deleted and reloaded: researcher"}
# Registry reloads automatically after delete.
# Telegram test after: "how does the sort algorithm work"
# → now routes through Groq LLM (no skill match) — you will see the
#   classifier log instead of the skill match log
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/skills/researcher
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
###
# Expect 200: array without researcher entry
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
###
# Expect 400: {"message":"Invalid skill definition: <parse error detail>"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: broken-skill
description: This frontmatter is never closed
trigger-patterns:
  - "broken.*"
(no closing --- and no system prompt)
###
# Skill IS created (201). The bad capability is silently excluded.
# Check logs for: WARN Unknown ToolCapability 'MEMORY_SEARCH_TYPO' in skill 'bad-caps'
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: bad-caps"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: bad-caps
description: Skill with an invalid tool-capability name
trigger-patterns:
  - "bad.*caps"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH_TYPO
max-iterations: 3
---
You are a test skill with a deliberately malformed capability.
